Wire `ReprAttr::ReprCpp` to `ReprFlags::IS_CPP | IS_C` during
`ReprOptions::from_attrs`.

Setting both bits makes every `repr.c()` check (dozens throughout
the compiler) answer true for `repr(cpp)` types — correct behavior
at the layout-level (no Rust reordering, defined ABI). The small
set of callers that need the C-vs-C++ distinction use `repr.cpp()`
added by P04.

